# Test vectors ported from simplefix (https://github.com/da4089/simplefix), MIT licence,
# Copyright (C) 2016-2026, David Arnold.
# Only behaviour checked by simplefix's own tests is ported. BodyLength(9) and CheckSum(10)
# of every validate/frame vector were recomputed with python3; fixes are noted per vector.
#
# Skipped (not representable or config-dependent):
#   test_parser.py::test_raw_data, test_raw_data_tags - raw data values contain SOH
#   test_parser.py::test_simplefix_on_split_execution_report - XmlData(213) holds embedded SOH
#   test_parser.py::test_stop_tag, test_stop_tag_deprecated, test_stop_char_*,
#     test_eol_is_eom_* - parser options (alternative stop tag / '\n' stop byte), no 10= trailer
#   test_parser.py::test_empty_value (parse) - accepted or rejected depending on parser option
#     allow_empty_values; only the framing of that message is ported
#   test_parser.py::test_parse_empty_string, test_begin_string_config - API/config only
#   test_message.py time/timestamp, compare, remove, repeating-group and tag/value type tests -
#     encoder API only, nothing tag=value-parsing related

# ---- parse ----

id = simplefix.basic_fix_message
source = da4089/simplefix:test/test_parser.py::test_basic_fix_message
kind = parse
msg = 8=FIX.4.2|9=10|35=D|29=A|10=203|
expect = ok
fields = 8=FIX.4.2|9=10|35=D|29=A|10=203|
note = FixMessage(8=FIX.4.2,35=D,29=A).encode() parsed back; 8, 35, 29 values recovered

id = simplefix.bad_tag
source = da4089/simplefix:test/test_parser.py::test_bad_tag
kind = parse
msg = 8=FIX.4.2|9=10|35=D|xx=A|10=203|
expect = error
note = non-numeric tag 'xx' raises TagNotNumberError

id = simplefix.int_value_zero
